{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Arnon.</b> Which Moab had possessed." "<b>Until the children of Ammon.</b> For it is written that half the land of the children of Ammon belonged to Israel, for they took it from the hand of the Amorite, who had first taken it from the hand of the children of Ammon. And Scripture states concerning Moab and Ammon that HaShem would not give of their land to Israel so much as the tread of the sole of a foot. The meaning is the land that was in their possession at that time; therefore Scripture needed to state the words of the rulers, on account of Heshbon, where Israel dwelt, for so it is written: \"And Israel dwelt in all the cities of the Amorite, in Heshbon.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:41.987988507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}